effect module EffectWhereCommentRun where { command = {- one -} {- two -} MyCmd, subscription {- three -} = MySub } exposing (..)

-- A RUN of comments written inside an effect module's `where { ... }` block,
-- left of a handler's constructor. The `where`, the `{`, the label keyword and
-- the `=` all carry no position in the AST, so there is no honest anchor for
-- any of them (see `mkZeroWidthText`'s anchoring policy) and every such comment
-- collapses to the one slot between `where` and `{` — the same canonical
-- rendering AmbiguousEffectModule pins for a single comment.
--
-- The run is what this fixture is for: the labels used to be anchored by
-- counting backwards from the constructor's column, which lands inside the
-- comments' own text once a comment sits in that gap, so a run of two was torn
-- across the `{` — one member outside it, one inside — and the reparse put them
-- back together. `{- three -}` pins the boundary: it is past the first
-- binding's constructor, so it stays inside the block, between the bindings.

import Task


type MyCmd msg
    = MyCmd (Task.Task Never msg)


type MySub msg
    = MySub Never
